\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.2}{\ignorespaces (a) Relative error of the central-difference tangent of \texttt  {Tet4NeoHookean} against the step, with the complex-step tangent as reference; the minimum is $1.6\times 10^{-11}$\xspace  {} near the step $3.2\times 10^{-6}$\xspace  {}. (b) Residual norm of the corrected Newton solve of the two-bar truss with and without the Jacobian of the correction in the tangent; the floor near $10^{-9}$\nobreakspace  {}N is rounding. (c) Relative difference between the adjoint gradient and a central difference of the whole solve against the step used in the difference; the rise at small steps is the convergence tolerance of Newton, the rise at large steps is the truncation of the difference. Generated by \texttt  {scripts/appA\_assets.py}.\relax }}{163}{figure.caption.271}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:df-checks}{{A.2}{163}{(a) Relative error of the central-difference tangent of \texttt {Tet4NeoHookean} against the step, with the complex-step tangent as reference; the minimum is \adaFdBest {} near the step \adaFdBestH {}. (b) Residual norm of the corrected Newton solve of the two-bar truss with and without the Jacobian of the correction in the tangent; the floor near $10^{-9}$~N is rounding. (c) Relative difference between the adjoint gradient and a central difference of the whole solve against the step used in the difference; the rise at small steps is the convergence tolerance of Newton, the rise at large steps is the truncation of the difference. Generated by \texttt {scripts/appA\_assets.py}.\relax }{figure.caption.271}{}}
